  "answer": "No past ticket reports this problem. The closest ones are different issues: #2795 and #4560 are about the filename format not being saved from the Settings UI (both fixed long ago), and #48909 is about locating the CLI executable. None describe the Image Resizer CLI ignoring -n/--filename on first run because Settings.Reload() saves defaults and caches _fileNameFormat. Your root-cause analysis looks specific and new, so keep this ticket open as a new bug. As a workaround until it is fixed, run the CLI once so settings.json is created, then rerun with --filename. The fix you suggested (clear _fileNameFormat in the FileName setter and mark FileNameFormat [JsonIgnore]) would be the way to resolve it."
